### 5.2 Fitting Algorithm and Parameters

In order to get a consistent set of parameters that describe the physical features at the moment of freeze-out, different sets of histograms are fitted simultaneously. At the stage of thermal freeze-out, all the hadrons and the light nuclei are already formed, and it is possible to use one set of parameters to fit all the \(p_{T}\) spectra and \(v_{2}\). The BW parameters are sensitive to different fitted quantities, _e.g._\(T\) is sensitive to the \(p_{T}\) spectra, and \(R_{x}/R_{y}\) is sensitive to \(v_{2}\) but not to \(p_{T}\) spectra, so it is necessary to use separate histograms to determine the various parameters of the BW model.

